n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/ca/cad0f92fdd888243562619b410a200ca040ca43f83bfd15fb124c8a8ecae4df6.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientation of the inner curve ${C}_{2}$ is opposite that of ${C}_{2}$ as stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}-\\left(- \\frac{19}{3}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{51-(-38)+(-2)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0015fc8-88b5-5637-806e-0694134e0bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543826} {:answer/id #uuid "bbea5b3d-93cf-5bdb-b3b9-dc8d398f6a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{47}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543830} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d1bfe2-984f-576e-a3ec-0532fcc4e3e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{47}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543833} {:answer/id #uuid "e971687d-bfd0-50d9-822f-623b570efa14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{89}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543835} {:answer/id #uuid "fa61e5ce-3036-5c2e-9dab-860447db6fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" 